# Agent lessons

Before spawning sibling agents, changing solvers, or claiming a milestone is done, read [docs/AGENT_LESSONS.md](../../docs/AGENT_LESSONS.md).

**Parallel work**

- Assume siblings may write into `/workspace` even when asked to use a worktree. Do not checkout/commit there while they run unless ownership is proven disjoint.
- Give each agent a disjoint path list. Serialize `CMakeLists.txt`, `tests/harness.hpp`, and `tests/unit/test_main.cpp`, or have only the parent touch them.
- Subagents often cannot `ManagePullRequest`; the parent opens PRs after push and subscribes CI.
- If the tree is interleaved: WIP snapshot branch, then path-checkout onto clean `cursor/<feature>-c006` branches from the correct base. Trim CMake/docs per branch before build.
- Re-run `git status` immediately before every commit; restore unexpected paths.

**Architecture / correctness (short)**

- On `main`, 3–4 card boards use `StreetBatchSolver`; 5 cards use `RiverBatchSolver`. Do not retire `river_solver` before five-card StreetBatch pins match `RiverGame`.
- Pin production batch changes against `CfrTrainer<*Game>` / `--reference`. Kuhn/Leduc stay on `CfrTrainer` only. `include/` must not depend on `ui/`.
- Nash gap is NashConv (sum of BR gains), not Pio’s averaged exploitability. Accuracy uses NashConv/pot.
- Own-reach averaging; CF regret uses opponent×chance; tiny compatible mass must not invent a uniform opponent; equity ≠ chip EV.
- Street config is `street-config 1` text; river explorer defaults are often JSON — do not mix formats. Empty bet arrays mean check-only; absent keys mean defaults.
- Do not change `LICENSE`. Update `FEATURE_PARITY.md` only with the commit that demonstrates the row.
